=== NVIDIA configured on the dev box
ok gst.vah264enc: /dev/dri/renderD128 is NVIDIA's, which has no VA-API encoder: recordings use x264 on the CPU
optional vaapi: /dev/dri/renderD128 (NVIDIA, config) · LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iHD
  → NVIDIA has no VA-API encoder: set encoder.vaapi_device in /home/me/.config/qrec/config.toml to an Intel or AMD render node, or remove it (Qrec then takes the first one)
VA-API render nodes: /dev/dri/renderD128 (NVIDIA 0x2db8), /dev/dri/renderD129 (Intel 0x7d51)
  set LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iHD (was nvidia)
  /dev/dri/renderD128 isn't probed: NVIDIA has no VA-API encoder (and VA-API on it can hang)

